 will now propose to curators","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/587"},{"number":748,"state":"open","title":"Cooked_Meat_Medium keeps FOODON:03305103 (the food) as its identity: the mint is blocked by two mixtures whose component references are pinned by the resolution component ledger","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/748"},{"number":750,"state":"closed","title":"Batch-3 hydrate_review notes cited a MediaDive compound id that was never verified","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/750"},{"number":344,"state":"closed","title":"9 hydrate labels state a hydration number with no known corresponding hydrate","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/344"},{"number":737,"state":"closed","title":"#245 ruling text: narrowMatch banner, unmeasured \"most\", and KGX_EXPORT cross-reference are inconsistent with the new contract","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/737"},{"number":363,"state":"closed","title":"Should `Cobalamine` be cyanocobalamin? Media practice says Co(III), the record's own fields do not","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/363"},{"number":734,"state":"closed","title":"KGX exporter and 2026-09-21 review bundle still project skos:broadMatch as biolink:subclass_of (#245 ruling)","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/734"},{"number":767,"state":"closed","title":"Track scoped ingredient mappings, registry annotations and KGX integration","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/767"},{"number":652,"state":"closed","title":"Clear the five locally actionable hydrate exactMatches still pointing at anhydrous terms","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/652"},{"number":321,"state":"closed","title":"26 hydrate-named records map to anhydrous terms; 10 terms absorb multiple distinct hydrates","url":"https://github.